        "original_id": "c88c516f-b67b-577b-85a4-a936741dd0cf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shengzhou, Linchuan District, Changle River, Dongyang, Daoshangling Mountain, Hangzhou Bay, Shaoxing, Fuzhou, Jiangxi, Zhejiang, China\n- Topics: administrative divisions, river geography\n\nFacts:\n- Shengzhou, formerly called Shengxian or Sheng County, is a county-level city in central Zhejiang, south of Hangzhou Bay, and forms the southeastern part of the prefecture-level city of Shaoxing.\n- Linchuan District is the only district of Fuzhou in Jiangxi province, People's Republic of China.\n- Changle River originates from Daoshangling Mountain in Dongyang, and Daoshangling Mountain has an elevation of 744 meters.\n- Changle River is known as Lüxi River and Heshan River in Shengzhou.",
